Every must-show item renders; no must-not-show item appears. Structurally this is a sound three-column grid — cards top-align at y=68, a uniform 4px gutter (x=917-920, 1529-1532), 9-10px inner padding — undermined by one column half empty beside one that is clipped.

Changes: (1) landed. The DATA note is a grid-spanning `dd` flush-left at x=1543, the labels' own left edge, six lines at ~52ch. The row spans y=189-363: 174px, 17.3% of the pane's 1007px, down from 39-41%. The gutter is no longer empty. (2) not observable — there is no `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` row in this view at all; the only cost row, `COST · MANA` (y=634), is base ten in one 30px row. (3) present in its no-call-data variant but misgrouped — see finding 2. (4) landed: `⊘` on line 29, `⊙` on line 32, both in the same 12px gutter column as the `·` on lines 26-28/31. (5) landed: the exit reads `← demo` (x=24-190).

Standing observation: half of it holds. Tabbed region y=68-669 (601px); content ends y=320; 348px empty = 57.9% of the card, 64% of the interior below the FRAME header. But Values does not overflow — y=674-1075, last separator y=952, 122px (30.4%) spare. Only Transaction overflows, clipped mid-JSON at y=1075. Middle column: 470 of 1007px blank, 46.7%.

Fixes: move the tabbed region's 348px to Values; lift the decoded-input note above the rule at y=876.

